**Key design decisions:**
- `ensure_parents` handles both intermediate and final components uniformly, which is exactly the `-p` semantic: every component must end up as a directory (or symlink-to-dir).
- Owner `wx` enforcement via `chmod` after `mkdir` ensures the "owner write and search permission ensured" requirement even under restrictive umasks.
- No `unlink`, `rmdir`, or `rename` calls — symlinks and non-directories are never replaced.
- `errno` is set on all failure paths so the caller can format a diagnostic with `strerror(errno)`.
- The operand-detection logic in Phase 2 is unified into a single `is_operand` determination to avoid duplicating the `-p` vs non-`-p` branch twice.
